From ca13b579d6f85a9deab32c5175223a3b572ccc6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lina <lokinyauv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 06:53:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(ui): don't let a second click reverse a power command
 mid-boot

A base station takes tens of seconds to spin up, and on hardware that
doesn't report its power state there is nothing to show for it in the
meantime. So the station looks like it ignored the click, the obvious
reaction is to click again - and because the app has already cached
the state it just wrote, that second click sends the opposite command
and the station stops partway through booting.

Seen in a live log: both stations were woken at 06:46:35, then put
back to sleep at 06:46:41, six seconds in.

Give the power controls the same cooldown the identify button already
uses, long enough to cover the spin-up.

(cherry picked from commit d1e1a75f7d6b73a2d84338142e6ceab4533cfcc6)
