From de1caa584bd170945e941fff98aebe7de41b1f15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lina <lokinyauv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 07:09:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(ui): replace the guessing power toggle with explicit
 on/off buttons

On Windows the power characteristic is write-only - it reports
properties 0x08, with no read and no notify. So power_state is -1
after every start and the app has no way to know whether a station is
on. A single toggle has to guess, and each guess broke one direction:

- Assuming unknown meant "off" sent "awake" on click, so stations
  could never be turned off.
- Assuming unknown meant "possibly on" sent "sleep" on click, so they
  could never be turned on. In a live log both stations got value 0
  while the user was trying to start them.

Writing to the characteristic works fine either way - a direct write
outside the app starts both stations - so the only defect was the
command the app picked.

Show a separate on and off button instead, everywhere a power control
exists (station row, group row, header). The app no longer guesses,
and the controls don't change meaning underneath the user.

The status dot still reports awake / asleep / unknown, and the 15s
cooldown still covers the spin-up so an early second press can't abort
a boot.

(cherry picked from commit f54df29062b110ad0ac943b4227d07e48a48fbda)
