From 3dfd2e730f43c5fc44aeed0d8277819860927a53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lina <lokinyauv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 07:23:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(ui): stop swallowing power presses, and report failed
 commands

The power controls held a flat 15s cooldown after every press. That
was added back when a single toggle meant a quick second click sent
the opposite command and aborted a boot - with separate on/off buttons
that hazard is gone, since pressing "on" twice just sends awake twice.
All the cooldown did was drop legitimate presses, and because each
control kept its own timer, which presses landed looked arbitrary.

Hold the guard only while the command is actually in flight, so
overlapping runs still can't race but the button frees up as soon as
the work is done. Verified: three presses three seconds apart now all
reach the base stations, where before only the first did.

Also surface failures. The ChangeBaseStationPowerStatus wrapper
awaited the call but never returned its result, so "error: base
station not connected" - which the Go side can take 30s of retrying to
decide - was dropped on the floor and a failed command looked exactly
like a swallowed one.

bulkUpdate returns the failures instead of reporting them itself: the
manual buttons show them, while the SteamVR automation only logs, so
no dialog can appear while the app sits unattended in the tray.

(cherry picked from commit afddfef9cf253852923db9ea30f530d42a3e00f3)
